    <string name="tip_en_end_of_tutorial">This is the end of the tutorial.</string>
    <string name="tip_en_to_close_keyboard">Press \"back\" (←) to close the keyboard.</string>
    <string name="tip_en_to_open_keyboard">The keyboard opens any time you touch a text field.</string>
    <string name="tip_to_step1">Like a normal mobile keyboard, tapping ○ three times will result\nin *C*.</string>
    <string name="tip_to_step2_a">For example, let\'s type \"hi.\"\n- Tap ○ twice to get \"h\"</string>
    <string name="tip_to_step2_b">\n- Tap → to advance to the right</string>
    <string name="tip_to_step2_c">\n- Tap ○ three times to get \"i\"</string>
    <string name="tip_to_step2_d">\n- Use touch or ↓ to set the word.</string>
    <string name="tip_to_step3_a">The ■ key switches between Japanese, English, and number input.</string>
    <string name="tip_to_step3_b">We\'ve switched from English to numbers. Next is Japanese.</string>
    <string name="tip_to_step3_c">Let\'s return to English now.</string>
    <string name="tip_to_step4">For other input modes (like full width)\nor a PC style keyboard, hold ■\nfor 3 seconds to show the input menu.</string>
    <string name="tip_to_step5">When you\'re done typing, hit the \"back\" key (←) to close the keyboard.</string>
    <string name="tip_to_step6">This is the end of the tutorial.</string>
    <string name="touch_to_continue">Next »</string>
